    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "cde50e155494e6dfd89e4ec356d99d0e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2062,
    "chunk_text": "Now, I would like to remind the President and the Government that our party, the All Ceylon Tamil Congress which I represent in Parliament and the oldest\n\n295 296\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf ]\n\n2024 \u0dc1\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 04\n\nTo talk in terms of racism, when the Tamils bring up the issues they have faced for over 75 years, in being deliberately targeted in areas where we have historically habited, where our ethnic composition has been systemically changed, altered by the State policies and when we rebel against those policies of the State, there is a potential for this last paragraph of the Hon. President's Address to Parliament to also be coined by this Government as racism. So, I would like clarifications because after 75 years of systematic anti-Tamilness in the North and the East, which are our areas of historical habitation, when we talk of discrimination and racism that have been meted out against us, to simply say that we must not talk about Tamils, Sinhalese and that we must talk of Sri Lankans is simply to erase that history of discrimination and racism that had been meted out for 75 years against the Tamil people; it is systematic racism. For example, Sir, in the UN Human Rights Council, Prince Zeid, who was the High Commissioner for Human Rights, made it a point that Sri Lanka cannot have an entirely internal inquiry for accountability because of the history of the ethnic conflict for over 35 years and that the institution of Government has been so corrupted that they cannot deliver justice, particularly in an ethnic-conflict sense. So, these are important realities that we must address, if we are to ever genuinely create security for all ethnicities, for the Tamil people, particularly who, they believe, have been discriminated against.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Member, you have only one more minute."
