    "md5": "01fc7385148b85d81f58fad0ecd35347",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1796,
    "chunk_text": "Let me unequivocally state that my presence here today is not to advocate division, but to champion unity, harmony and prosperity of this beautiful nation. The mandate from our people is resoundingly clear. We must move forward as one cohesive entity undeterred by ethnic or religious prejudices and strive together towards a shared vision of peace and development.\n\nFrom my first posting as a doctor to the Base Hospital, Chavakachcheri after my internship at Kalubowila Teaching Hospital to my tenure as a medical administrator, I have witnessed stark inequities and systemic corruption that plague our healthcare system, particularly in the Northern and the Eastern Provinces. My tenure as Director of the Base Hospital, Chavakachcheri was marked by significant reforms achieved within just three days, but those efforts were met\n\n309 310\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nwith staunch resistance from entrenched interests. My exposure of corrupt practices led to my unwarranted imprisonment for 19 days, a sobering reminder of the immense challenges faced by those who stand against systemic corruption. Yet, it was the unwavering support of the public that shielded me from the darker machinations of my political opponents.\n\nContesting this Parliamentary seat independently, without the backing of established political parties, I stand here today as a testament to the resilience of our people, who demand for accountability, equity and meaningful reform. Hon. Members, as we stand at a crossroads of history, we must confront the lingering wounds of our past with courage, clarity and genuine commitment to reconciliation.\n\nThe Prevention of Terrorism Act, a relic of a wounded, troubled and painful era, must be repealed to restore justice and freedom to those unjustly detained."
  },
