    "chunk_text": "The first one is of particular concern, Sir. In 2016, with World Bank funding of US Dollars 55 million, the Strategic Cities Development Project - SCDP - commenced. That Project was completed without the participation of the Jaffna Divisional Secretariat and the Nallur Divisional Secretariat because the sort of project overlapped from Jaffna and Nallur. The Jaffna UDA was kept out and the Jaffna Municipal Council was also completely kept out. Instead, the implementation of the project was by the UDA Head Office in Colombo. Particularly, the SCDP Management Unit and the SCDP Implementation Unit were formed with persons who did not have any adequate qualifications, as they were political appointees. The master plan for the drainage system implemented under that project was to be drawn up and prepared with a funding of Rs. 1,870 million. That was allocated to a private firm by the UDA in Colombo, but the plan was made without rainfall data or elevation data. Sir, that matter was brought to the attention of those implementation committees and questions were raised by well-meaning experts who happened to be observers and who had heard about this oversight, a deliberate oversight is what we can say. But, they were completely ignored and the plan went through.\n\nThat project was started in 2016. So, you can just imagine why it was hushed up. Therefore, I would urge this Government to look into that.\n\nThe second matter I want to raise relates to Batticaloa in particular. We were visiting Batticaloa around the 26th\n\nand the 27th of November and the complaint we got right across the region, despite the fact that there is a problem with drainage, lack of it et cetera, was because of the rainfall being so heavy, all the sluice gates in those tanks were opened at the same time and as a result, the water just could not be controlled. There was no coordination and that was another very important reason why Batticaloa faced such a calamity over the last few days."
