    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "fe7fb70c38d74a05557508ed4c2a43e2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2161,
    "chunk_text": "our unstinted support to ensure that you carry out and discharge that responsibility to the best of your ability. You have been elected as the Speaker of the entire Parliament and I am sure that you would discharge that responsibility to the best of your ability. I wish you all the best on behalf of the United National Party and the NDF!\n\nSir, I would like to wish you strength and wisdom in conducting the Proceedings in a fair and equitable manner. You have been appointed at a very crucial period, where we are recovering from our economic crisis. Also, amidst one of the largest single-party majorities this country has witnessed, the degree of equity should be higher.\n\nOnce again, Sir, I would like to wish you all the best and we would provide you with our fullest support.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Speaker) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dda\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dda\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dd3\u0dc0.\u0dd3\u0dc0. \u0daf\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4 \u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Speaker, I would like to take this opportunity to congratulate you. But, at the same time, I must also say that I do not envy your job because you are a Member of a party which has just been elected with over a two-thirds majority and coming from that party and taking up the position of the Speaker means that you must disregard that mandate to some extent because your job here is not about that mandate, but rather to safeguard the interests of every single Member of Parliament and also be fair by all parties present in this Parliament disregarding their mandates.\n\nSir, in that respect, I would like to urge you to learn from the mistakes of the previous Parliament, which also had a two-thirds majority, but where minor parties were not given adequate hearing and chances because the previous Parliament chose to stick to outdated Standing Orders not reflecting particularly the composition of the Opposition of that Parliament."
  },
