    "chunk_text": "Otherwise, it is illegal and unconstitutional. If it is a sovereign debt which we all are bound by, bankruptcy must be declared by Parliament. But, all the oversight Committees, the then Opposition as well as the Hon. Members at that particular moment in Parliament had overlooked that fact.\n\nSo, the story goes on. On the 01st of September, 2022, the Staff-level Agreement between the IMF and the Government is reached to check debt sustainability and to decide on the way forward for the restructuring of debt. On the 20th of February, 2023, the IMF team comes to Colombo and sits down for discussions with the Government of Sri Lanka and ensures that debt restructuring and debt sustainability is looked at for their viability. Then, on the 20th of March, 2023, the IMF approves the Agreement. Later, it is brought to Parliament, debated and voted on. Then, the Extended Fund Facility - EFF - effectively comes into place. That basically bestows on the Government almost US Dollars 3 billion or SDR 2.286 billion, which is the specific deposit to be reserved and utilized under a 48-month programme. So, that is the start of the IMF programme which comes into effect from the 20th of March, 2023.\n\nDebt restructuring has been in three stages. The first stage was Domestic Debt Restructuring, which happened on the 01st of July, 2023, where the domestic debt was looked at and a solution was provided. There were weak points which could be looked at and debated, but finally, that particular first step was taken with the least impact. Then, the second was, bilateral and multilateral debt. The Paris Club and the countries which are not in the Paris Club, all got together with the Official Creditor Committee co-chaired by Japan and India under the"
