    "md5": "d9830145d39b61637f76c4bad48fcc2d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 991,
    "chunk_text": "Then, the third stage was the most difficult aspect, having to deal with commercial creditors including international sovereign bond holders and the China Development Bank. On the 19th of September, 2024, just two days before the Presidential Election, they come into an agreement in principle and with that, the then Government signs the Agreement two days before the election. It was thought that that was a deal, an election \"gundu\u201d made just before the Presidential Election. Finally, it was proven that it was a done deal. Then, the Government changed.\n\n1189 1190\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd2 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0ddc\u0db1\u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc]\n\n2024 \u0dc1\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 17\n\nThe Government changed and then, the IMF and the Hamilton Reserve Bank was informed on the 01st of November, 2024 by the new Government that they would still pursue the same process adopted by the Wickremesinghe Government. Then, on the 12th of December, 2024, we had the restructuring of Macro-linked Bonds concluded."
